You're not here to debate, you're definitely not here to win, you are here to maintain

1353
01:59:05,580 --> 01:59:10,320
the flow, enforce the rules, protect the host, and protect the community.

1354
01:59:10,900 --> 01:59:13,660
Think of our child like a dining room in a fine restaurant.

1355
01:59:14,400 --> 01:59:17,460
Most guests are polite and having a good time.

1356
01:59:18,100 --> 01:59:19,540
Some might get a little out.

1357
01:59:19,950 --> 01:59:24,470
And then there's that one guy in the corner trying to light the napkins on fire.

1358
01:59:24,970 --> 01:59:26,530
That's where you come in.

1359
01:59:27,270 --> 01:59:30,410
Your job is to handle the situation quickly and quietly,

1360
01:59:30,750 --> 01:59:33,570
so everyone else can keep enjoying their meal.

1361
01:59:34,350 --> 01:59:38,890
To do this effectively, we follow our core values, the 3 Cs.

1362
01:59:39,590 --> 01:59:41,870
Come consistent and clear.

1363
01:59:42,540 --> 01:59:43,980
Let's break it down.

1364
01:59:44,600 --> 01:59:45,280
First calm.

1365
01:59:45,880 --> 01:59:51,740
If someone bursts into the chat typing in all cups, that the tarot is fake, and the moon

1366
01:59:51,740 --> 01:59:53,520
is a government drone just brief.

1367
01:59:54,160 --> 01:59:57,460
You are not required to correct their version of reality.

1368
01:59:58,220 --> 02:00:01,120
Your job isn't to be a fact-checker for the universe.

1369
02:00:01,880 --> 02:00:04,960
Simply delete the disruptive message and move on.

1370
02:00:09,310 --> 02:00:15,710
Your energy sets the tone. Panicking or reacting emotionally only adds fuel to the fire.

1371
02:00:16,470 --> 02:00:19,710
Stay calm, stay detached, and keep the peace.

1372
02:00:20,510 --> 02:00:22,190
Next, we have consistent.

1373
02:00:22,920 --> 02:00:24,860
This is absolutely key.

1374
02:00:25,480 --> 02:00:31,460
If one person gets timed out for harassment, then everyone who engages in harassment gets

1375
02:00:31,460 --> 02:00:32,120
timed out.

1376
02:00:32,620 --> 02:00:36,020
We don't moderate based on our personal feelings or vibes.

1377
02:00:36,640 --> 02:00:37,960
We don't play favorites.

1378
02:00:38,660 --> 02:00:41,820
We moderate based on behavior, pure and simple.

1379
02:00:42,500 --> 02:00:46,060
The rules apply equally to everyone, every single time.

1380
02:00:50,360 --> 02:00:55,260
Viewers learn what to expect and feel secure knowing the environment is fair and predictable.

1381
02:00:56,000 --> 02:00:57,340
And finally, clear.

1382
02:00:57,930 --> 02:01:01,830
The rules are always posted and visible for everyone to see.

1383
02:01:02,230 --> 02:01:05,410
The expectations are laid out right there in the open.

1384
02:01:05,970 --> 02:01:08,910
There are no secret punishments or surprise rules.

1385
02:01:09,590 --> 02:01:14,570
Everything we do is fair, predictable, and frankly, a little bit boring.

1386
02:01:15,190 --> 02:01:18,770
And in the world of chat moderation, boring is good.

1387
02:01:19,530 --> 02:01:20,510
Boring means stable.

1388
02:01:21,430 --> 02:01:22,250
Boring means safe.

1389
02:01:22,800 --> 02:01:28,360
It means the focus stays on the content in the community, not on drama in the chat.

1390
02:01:29,100 --> 02:01:31,080
Come consistent clear.

1391
02:01:31,880 --> 02:01:34,360
The three pillars of a healthy digital space.

1392
02:01:35,300 --> 02:01:37,220
Now let's talk about your tools.

1393
02:01:38,060 --> 02:01:41,640
These are the buttons you'll use to keep the chat running smoothly.

1394
02:01:42,320 --> 02:01:45,900
Think of them as your utility belt for digital peacekeeping.

1395
02:01:46,500 --> 02:01:48,340
First up is the DELETE button.

1396
02:01:48,920 --> 02:01:54,200
This is your go-to for simple spam, repeated nonsense, or any mild disruptions.

1397
02:01:54,780 --> 02:01:58,580
Someone posting the same emoji over and over, DELETE.

1398
02:01:59,220 --> 02:02:03,260
A message that's slightly off-topic, but not aggressive, DELETE.

1399
02:02:03,920 --> 02:02:05,080
It's the lightest touch.

1400
02:02:05,540 --> 02:02:07,480
A gentle sweep to keep things tidy.

1401
02:02:10,120 --> 02:02:13,080
Think of this as a five-minute cooldown period.

1402
02:02:13,680 --> 02:02:16,120
This tool is for escalating behavior.

1403
02:02:16,750 --> 02:02:23,050
If someone ignores a gentle nudge or continues to be disruptive after a message was deleted,

1404
02:02:23,650 --> 02:02:27,410
a timeout gives them a moment to pause and reflect on the roles.

1405
02:02:27,950 --> 02:02:33,070
It's a clear signal that their behavior is crossing a line without permanently removing

1406
02:02:33,070 --> 02:02:33,390
them.

1407
02:02:33,930 --> 02:02:36,750
It's a temporary measure for a temporary problem.

1408
02:02:37,350 --> 02:02:39,790
And then, there's the hide user button.

1409
02:02:45,630 --> 02:02:51,810
or repeated violations after a timeout. Hiding a user from the channel removes their ability

1410
02:02:51,810 --> 02:02:59,270
to comment permanently. Remember this critical point, you are not silencing opinions. You are

1411
02:03:01,290 --> 02:03:04,510
We welcome a wide range of opinions and discussions.

1412
02:03:05,370 --> 02:03:10,230
We do not welcome personal attacks or behavior that makes others feel unsafe.

1413
02:03:10,990 --> 02:03:13,470
Your job is to distinguish between the two.

1414
02:03:14,010 --> 02:03:16,890
Use your tolls wisely, and you'll be a pro.

1415
02:03:17,610 --> 02:03:22,370
Ah, and now it's time to meet a special character you'll encounter, the troll.

1416
02:03:26,960 --> 02:03:34,280
It feeds on attention, it loves arguments, and it absolutely savers any emotional reaction you give it.

1417
02:03:34,860 --> 02:03:37,340
The more you engage, the stronger it gets.

1418
02:03:38,120 --> 02:03:40,640
However, the troll has a few weaknesses.

1419
02:03:41,380 --> 02:03:47,320
It does not feed on silence, it starves in the face of swift moderation, and it withers

1420
02:03:47,320 --> 02:03:49,040
when it is completely ignored.

1421
02:03:49,620 --> 02:03:54,220
If a troll appears and the chat starts arguing with it, you may need to step in.

1422
02:03:54,760 --> 02:04:01,120
A simple, gentle message like, hey everyone, let's stay on topic, can help redirect the

1423
02:04:01,120 --> 02:04:01,760
conversation.

1424
02:04:06,640 --> 02:04:08,200
Do not debate the troll.

1425
02:04:08,940 --> 02:04:11,000
Do not try to educate the troll.

1426
02:04:11,700 --> 02:04:14,600
And please, do not try to psychoanalyze the troll.

1427
02:04:15,380 --> 02:04:18,060
You are not a counselor or a therapist.

1428
02:04:18,790 --> 02:04:20,570
You are quality control.

1429
02:04:21,170 --> 02:04:25,270
Your only job is to remove the disruption and let the troll go hungry.

1430
02:04:25,870 --> 02:04:29,250
One of your most important duties is protecting the host.

1431
02:04:29,910 --> 02:04:35,490
During live readings or focus segments, the host must be able to concentrate completely.

1432
02:04:36,230 --> 02:04:39,750
Their energy needs to be on the reading, not on distractions.

1433
02:04:46,560 --> 02:04:50,880
If the person continues, use a timeout or hide them from the channel.

1434
02:04:51,580 --> 02:04:54,060
Never allow a smear to linger on the screen.

1435
02:04:54,580 --> 02:04:59,660
A lie that is left visible, even for a few seconds, becomes a distraction.

1436
02:05:00,400 --> 02:05:03,260
A distraction can quickly derail the entire show.

1437
02:05:03,800 --> 02:05:06,360
And derailment hurts the experience for everyone.

1438
02:05:07,140 --> 02:05:12,520
By keeping the check clean, you protect the host's focus and the integrity of the content.

1439
02:05:14,720 --> 02:05:17,720
So, how do you decide which tool to use?

1440
02:05:18,460 --> 02:05:20,880
Let's talk about our escalation protocol.

1441
02:05:21,740 --> 02:05:27,280
It's a simple, step-by-step process for SIX is almost always to delete the offending

1442
02:05:27,280 --> 02:05:27,680
message.

1443
02:05:28,580 --> 02:05:30,960
It's a clean, simple first action.

1444
02:05:31,630 --> 02:05:35,910
If the behavior continues, you move to step 2, time out.

1445
02:05:36,470 --> 02:05:40,190
This gives the user a temporary break and a clear warning.

1446
02:05:40,790 --> 02:05:46,230
If they return and continue to violate the rules, you move to step 3, hide user.

1447
02:05:46,850 --> 02:05:51,570
This is the permanent solution for someone who refuses to respect the community guidelines.

1448
02:05:52,330 --> 02:05:56,850
Now, you are empowered to skip steps if a violation is severe enough.

1449
02:05:57,610 --> 02:06:00,050
Some actions warrant an immediate hide.

1450
02:06:00,490 --> 02:06:07,270
Examples include hate speech, personal threats, repeated and malicious slander, or any kind

1451
02:06:07,270 --> 02:06:09,730
