1452
02:06:10,470 --> 02:06:13,750
In these cases, you do not need to issue a warning.

1453
02:06:14,270 --> 02:06:17,110
You act decisively to protect the community.

1454
02:06:17,770 --> 02:06:21,770
We are firm when we need to be, but we are never dramatic about it.

1455
02:06:22,210 --> 02:06:26,190
Just as important as knowing what to do is knowing what not to do.

1456
02:06:26,710 --> 02:06:28,030
These are the hard-nose.

1457
02:06:28,690 --> 02:06:31,970
Do not argue publicly with other moderators in the chat.

1458
02:06:32,670 --> 02:06:34,870
Do not threaten users with punishments.

1459
02:06:35,510 --> 02:06:39,010
Do not mock someone's unstable or aggressive behavior.

1460
02:06:39,520 --> 02:06:44,680
Do not make a big show of announcing punishments like typing bye-bye troll.

1461
02:06:45,460 --> 02:06:49,280
And never ever turn moderation into your own personal performance.

1462
02:06:50,080 --> 02:06:53,280
The best moderation should feel almost invisible.

1463
02:06:53,900 --> 02:06:59,960
When you're doing your job right, most people in the chat won't even notice the disruptions

1464
02:06:59,960 --> 02:07:06,420
